   "metadata": {
    "id": "welcome_header"
   },
   "source": [
    "# 🚀 Harvest AI: GPU-Accelerated Video Processing\n",
    "\n",
    "Welcome to the **Harvest AI Colab Notebook**! This notebook enables you to run the complete AI Shorts video creation pipeline on high-performance Google Cloud GPUs (T4, L4, or A100), yielding up to **10x faster processing speeds** for AI transcription, active speaker face tracking, and video rendering.\n",
    "\n",
    "### ⚡ Key Features Enabled in Colab GPU Mode:\n",
    "1. **Whisper Transcription** (`faster-whisper`) accelerated with CUDA & `float16` precision.\n",
    "2. **YOLO Person Detection** (`ultralytics`) using GPU tensor cores.\n",
    "3. **Face Mesh Active-Speaker Tracking** (`mediapipe`).\n",
    "4. **Local LLM Engine** (`Ollama` + `Qwen 2.5`) running locally on Colab's GPU for smart highlight analysis and prompt translations — no OpenRouter API key needed!\n",
    "\n",
    "---"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "step1_header"
   },
   "source": [
    "## 🛠️ Step 1: Verify GPU Acceleration\n",
    "\n",
    "Before running the code, confirm that Google Colab is using a GPU backend:\n",
    "1. Go to **Runtime** > **Change runtime type** in the top menu.\n",
    "2. Select **T4 GPU** (or L4 / A100 if available) under *Hardware accelerator*.\n",
    "3. Click **Save**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "check_gpu_cell"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Verify GPU availability in PyTorch and list hardware specifications\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "\n",
    "gpu_available = torch.cuda.is_available()\n",
    "print(\"=\" * 50)\n",
    "print(f"🌟 GPU Acceleration Available: {gpu_available}")\n",
    "if gpu_available:\n",
    "    print(f"🎬 Device Name: {torch.cuda.get_device_name(0)}")\n",
    "    print(f"💾 Memory Allocated: {torch.cuda.memory_allocated(0) / 1024**2:.2f} MB")\n",
    "    print(\"=\" * 50)\n",
    "    !nvidia-smi\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"⚠️ WARNING: GPU is not active!\")\n",
    "    print(\"Please go to Runtime -> Change runtime type, select GPU, and try again.\")\n",
    "    print(\"=\" * 50)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "step2_header"
   },
   "source": [
    "## 📂 Step 2: Mount Google Drive & Upload Codebase\n",
    "\n",
    "Mount your Google Drive to load input videos and store the output videos. After running the cell below, zip your local `harvest_AI` project directory and upload it directly."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "mount_drive_cell"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Mount Google Drive\n",
    "from google.colab import drive\n",
    "drive.mount('/content/drive')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "upload_code_cell"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Upload and unzip the harvest_AI codebase zip file\n",
    "from google.colab import files\n",
    "import os\n",
    "\n",
    "target_dir = '/content/harvest_AI'\n",
    "\n",
    "if not os.path.exists(target_dir):\n",
    "    print(\"📤 Please upload the 'harvest_AI.zip' file containing the project's backend and assets.\")\n",
    "    uploaded = files.upload()\n",
    "    for filename in uploaded.keys():\n",
    "        if filename.endswith('.zip'):\n",
    "            print(f'Unzipping {filename} to {target_dir}...')\n",
    "            !unzip -q {filename} -d /content/\n",
    "            print(\"✅ Codebase successfully extracted!\")\n",
    "            break\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"✅ codebase directory 'harvest_AI' already exists at:\", target_dir)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "step3_header"
   },
   "source": [
    "## 📦 Step 3: Install Core Dependencies\n",
    "\n",
    "Install the required libraries for OpenCV, PyTorch, Whisper, YOLO, DeepSort, and MediaPipe."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "install_dependencies_cell"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Install FFmpeg system library and project Python requirements\n",
    "!apt-get update -qq && apt-get install -y -qq ffmpeg\n",
    "\n",
    "# Change directory to backend folder\n",
    "%cd /content/harvest_AI/backend\n",
    "\n",
    "# Install dependencies from requirements.txt\n",
    "!pip install -q -r requirements.txt\n",
    "print(\"\\n✅ Python dependencies installed successfully!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "step4_header"
   },
   "source": [
    "## 🦙 Step 4: Run Ollama & Setup Qwen 2.5 Locally on GPU\n",
    "\n",
    "To support smart highlight extraction and translation without external API costs, we will install Ollama and run a local `qwen2.5` language model directly on Colab's GPU."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "start_ollama_cell"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 1. Download and install Ollama\n",
    "!curl -fsSL https://ollama.com/install.sh | sh\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Launch the Ollama background daemon\n",
    "import subprocess\n",
    "import time\n",
    "import os\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"🚀 Launching Ollama daemon in background...\")\n",
    "# Directing output logs to ollama.log\n",
    "with open(\"ollama.log\", \"w\") as f:\n",
    "    subprocess.Popen([\"ollama\", \"serve\"], stdout=f, stderr=f)\n",
    "\n",
    "time.sleep(5)  # Let the daemon boot up\n",
    "\n",
    "# 3. Pull the Qwen 2.5 model (7B instruction-tuned)\n",
    "print(\"📥 Pulling Qwen 2.5 Model (4.7 GB)... This may take 1-2 minutes.\")\n",
    "!ollama pull qwen2.5\n",
    "print(\"✅ Ollama configuration complete!\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "step5_header"
   },
   "source": [
    "## 🔍 Step 5: Download YOLO Weights & Verify Directories\n",
    "\n",
    "Prepare the system directories and download the YOLO model weights if they aren't packaged in the ZIP file."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "setup_assets_cell"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import urllib.request\n",
    "\n",
    "# Ensure uploads and assets paths exist\n",
    "os.makedirs(\"/content/harvest_AI/backend/uploads\", exist_ok=True)\n",
    "os.makedirs(\"/content/harvest_AI/assets/music\", exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Check/Download YOLO weights\n",
    "yolo_path = \"/content/harvest_AI/backend/yolo11n.pt\"\n",
    "if not os.path.exists(yolo_path):\n",
    "    print(\"📥 Model weight yolo11n.pt missing. Downloading...\")\n",
    "    urllib.request.urlretrieve(\n",
    "        \"https://github.com/ultralytics/assets/releases/download/v8.3.0/yolo11n.pt\", \n",
    "        yolo_path\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    print(\"✅ YOLO model loaded successfully.\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"✅ YOLO model already present.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "step6_header"
   },
   "source": [
    "## 🎬 Step 6: Process Video (Run Master Agent)\n",
    "\n",
    "Use this cell to execute the Master Agent. Point it to a video stored in your Google Drive (e.g. `/content/drive/MyDrive/my_video.mp4`) or direct upload path."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "run_pipeline_cell"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "import os\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. Point paths properly\n",
    "backend_path = \"/content/harvest_AI/backend\"\n",
    "sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(backend_path, \"app\"))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Import services from app\n",
    "from app.services.master_agent import master_agent\n",
    "\n",
    "# =========================================================\n",
    "# CONFIGURATION PARAMETERS\n",
    "# =========================================================\n",
    "# Specify the input video path. \n",
    "# Change this to match your video path in Google Drive!\n",
    "INPUT_VIDEO_PATH = \"/content/drive/MyDrive/test_video.mp4\"\n",
    "TARGET_LENGTH = 15.0     # Max short length (seconds)\n",
    "PLATFORM = \"youtube\"     # Options: 'youtube' | 'tiktok' | 'instagram'\n",
    "EDITING_PROMPT = \"Make it highly viral. Zoom in on active speaker, add upbeat music, and translate captions if needed.\"\n",
    "# =========================================================\n",
    "\n",
    "if not os.path.exists(INPUT_VIDEO_PATH):\n",
    "    print(f\"❌ ERROR: Video file not found at: {INPUT_VIDEO_PATH}\")\n",
    "    print(\"Please upload a video or update the INPUT_VIDEO_PATH coordinate.\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f\"🔥 Running Master AI Agent Pipeline for video: {INPUT_VIDEO_PATH}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"📐 Settings: Length={TARGET_LENGTH}s, Platform={PLATFORM}\")\n",
    "    print(f\"💬 Prompt: '{EDITING_PROMPT}'\\n\")\n",
    "    \n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        # Execute Master Agent\n",
    "        shorts = master_agent.generate_shorts(\n",
    "            video_path=INPUT_VIDEO_PATH,\n",
    "            length=TARGET_LENGTH,\n",
    "            platform=PLATFORM,\n",
    "            optional_prompt=EDITING_PROMPT\n",
    "        )\n",
    "        \n",
    "        print(\"\\n🎉 === Processing Complete! ===\")\n",
    "        print(f\"Generated {len(shorts)} short variation(s):\")\n",
    "        for idx, short_clip in enumerate(shorts, 1):\n",
    "            print(f\"{idx}. {short_clip}\")\n",
    "            \n",
    "    except Exception as e:\n",
    "        print(f\"\\n❌ Processing failed with error: {e}\")\n",
    "        import traceback\n",
    "        traceback.print_exc()"
   ]
  },
  {
